WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:03.420
Scientists are using hydrogels,

00:00:03.420 --> 00:00:04.900
which are gels mostly made up of water,

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:08.410
to make the next generation of soft electronics

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:10.349
and soft robots.

00:00:10.349 --> 00:00:12.030
Their inspiration is nature,

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:15.400
where hydrogels abound.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:18.090
We are mostly a hydrogel--from our tissues

00:00:18.090 --> 00:00:19.910
and muscles to our brain.

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:22.810
How our softer parts combine with harder materials

00:00:22.810 --> 00:00:25.850
like our bones and teeth makes us special.

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:28.560
In the lab, there are many advantages

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:30.800
to using synthetic hydrogels.

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:34.180
After all, they squash, stretch and adapt

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:35.180
like animals and humans do.

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:39.220
But the trick is how to attach hydrogels

00:00:39.230 --> 00:00:42.780
onto all kinds of materials the way our bodies can.

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:44.940
Now researchers have come up with a fast

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:47.820
and simple method to form an instant tough bond

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:50.400
between hydrogels and a variety of

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:52.220
soft to hard materials.

00:00:52.220 --> 00:00:55.240
Others have tried to use pure Cyanoacrylates,

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:57.640
the main ingredient found in super glue,

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:00.460
but they form brittle, non-stretchable layers.

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:05.000
Instead, the team’s new method uses a glue

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:08.940
made up of cyanoacrylate diluted with a non-solvent.

00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:12.280
They spread this mixture onto tough hydrogels.

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:13.540
Mixed with the non-solvent,

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:15.460
the adhesive doesn’t dissolve,

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:19.310
which allows for a very thin layer of glue to form.

00:01:19.310 --> 00:01:21.940
This protective shell, delays polymerization

00:01:21.940 --> 00:01:24.160
just long enough, so when the materials

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:25.940
are slightly pressed together,

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:28.400
the non-solvent helps transport the glue

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:31.020
into the layers as it evaporates,

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:33.710
resulting in an instant tough bond.

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:38.820
Here, a hydrogel and an elastomer, a rubbery material,

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:41.120
are combined together with the new glue.

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:43.060
You can stretch them by 1000%

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:44.840
and they still don’t come apart.

00:01:45.180 --> 00:01:47.380
And the layer of glue is so thin,

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:49.940
that it doesn’t disturb the mechanics of the materials.

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:51.560
In peel tests,

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:54.320
Even with the toughest hydrogels used,

00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:57.750
the gel itself cracks but not the area where

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:00.500
the two materials were actually bonded together.

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:03.460
Next, researchers built several prototypes

00:02:03.660 --> 00:02:04.620
using this glue.

00:02:04.740 --> 00:02:08.640
An electronic skin complete with battery, bluetooth,

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:11.650
processor, heaters, and temperature sensors.

00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:14.170
The components are bonded onto a hydrogel,

00:02:14.170 --> 00:02:16.320
which wraps around the skin.

00:02:16.889 --> 00:02:18.560
Because hydrogels are permeable,

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:21.680
you could deliver water-soluble drugs through the gel

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:24.120
to the surface of the skin.

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:26.360
Hydrogel disc replacement in the spine

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:28.020
is already happening.

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:29.989
But with the new adhesive you could assemble

00:02:29.989 --> 00:02:33.200
this mix of hard and soft structures much more quickly.

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:37.000
So with tough hydrogels and this new super glue,

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:39.510
we could see a wave of soft technologies

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:42.499
and soft robots that are even more life-like.

00:02:42.499 --> 00:02:44.659
The speed and simplicity of the process allows

00:02:44.659 --> 00:02:46.319
for rapid prototyping,

00:02:46.319 --> 00:02:49.169
which is great news for the exploding DIY community

00:02:49.169 --> 00:03:02.889
of softbot makers.

